dd_library(SHARED)`, Cargo only `crate-type=[\"cdylib\"]` |\n| Feature combos | no `[features]`; ran default + `--no-default-features` × debug + release → 29/29 each |\n\nArtifacts in `translation/`: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, `tests/differential.rs`, `tests/feature_matrix.sh`. Both `.so`s are loaded via `libloading` and called only through `dlsym`, so the `#[no_mangle]` wrapper is under test.\n\nTwo subtleties I confirmed against the compiled C rather than assuming — both were my test's wrong predictions, not translation bugs:\n\n- **Negative shift count wraps, not saturates.** For `exp_q2 < 0`, `1 << 30 >> (e >> 2)` is UB in C; gcc emits `sar %cl`, count mod 32. So `ldexp_q2(1.0f, -4) == 0.0` but `ldexp_q2(1.0f, -124) == 0.5` and `ldexp_q2(1.0f, -128) == 1.0`. The Rust's `(e >> 2) & 31` reproduces this exactly.\n- **`exp_q2 == 0` is the identity.** The do/while body always runs once, and `9.31322575e-10f` rounds to exactly `2^-30`, so `g_expfrac[0] * (1<<30)` is exactly `1.0f`. Tests now pin this so a 1-ulp constant change would be caught.\n\nAlso verified faithful: `e & 3` two's-complement indexing (never out of bounds for negative `e`), `INT_MIN` not overflowing `exp_q2 -= e`, `INT_MAX`'s ~17.9M-iteration loop, and NaN payload/sign propagation including sNaN quieting.\n\nI did not modify `c_src/`. One note: `cargo` can't reach crates.io through the proxy, so all commands need `--offline` (`libloading 0.8.9` was already in the local registry cache).","ttft_ms":2503,"type":"result","duration_ms":603365,"uuid":"6c65ec32-2053-4682-b251-ca73f7e34042","ttft_stream_ms":2226,"time_to_request_ms":51,"first_content_frame_ms":2226,"queued_turn_count":0}
